      "title": "Import",
      "members": [],
      "paragraphs": [
        "Moves its actor to a destination, or after a moving target, through any NavigationSpace: it plans the route, progresses along its waypoints, slows down onto the destination, notices when the route goes stale and plans again.",
        "An agent decides where to go; a NavigationMovement performs the motion. It never touches the actor's transform itself, so the same agent drives a physics-backed movement, one that writes a node position, or one the game provides. Positions, destinations and targets are all read in the navigation space's coordinates.",
        "It steers in its fixed update, which a scene runs before its systems, so a movement backed by a physics world registered as a scene system receives each step's command before that world steps. Nothing is searched every step: a route is planned on a new command and replanned only when it went stale - the space's revision changed, a followed target moved to another node, a budget-limited partial route ran out, or the actor made no progress - and automatic replans are at most one per NavigationAgentOptions.repathInterval.",
        "Disabling the component stops the movement and keeps the command; enabling it again plans a fresh route to it. Pausing the scene pauses it."
      ],
      "importLine": "import { NavigationAgentComponent } from '@codexo/exojs/pathfinding'",
      "sourceLink": null
    },
